      "tier": 4,
      "name": "untrusted_template_chrome_and_truncated_tails",
      "trust_level": "Zero; never extract standalone facts or override Tiers 1-3.",
      "assignment_rule": "Assign to CMS template boilerplate, blank registration form inputs/dropdowns (school lists in nyu-07, nyu-10), LibCal's hardcoded 'Please note this is an online event' footer on in-person pages (nyu-07, nyu-10, nyu-12), reused media filenames (Scaramucci filename in nyu-05), and cut-off trailing tokens in truncated feeds (col-03, col-05)."
    }
  ],
  "identity_rules": [
    {
      "entity_type": "Place",
      "rule": "Separate room/floor text into Event.location_detail first so multiple rooms resolve to one building (uniting Rm. 619 in nyu-07, Rm. 743 in nyu-10, and Rm. 745 in nyu-14 as 'Bobst Library'). Merge two Place records within the same university if they share (a) the same feed location_id (nyu-05, nyu-15), (b) the same normalized street number and street name ('370 Jay Street' and '370 Jay St' in nyu-04; '601 W. 125th St.' uniting 'The Lee C. Bollinger Forum' and 'The Forum at Columbia University' in col-07, while keeping '181 Mercer Street' in nyu-02 distinct from '196 Mercer Street' in nyu-09), or (c) an alias co-declared on an official page ('Dibner Library' and 'Bern Dibner Library' in nyu-12; 'International Affairs Building' and 'IAB' in col-05). Never create a Place for 'Online Online' (col-03)."
    },
    {
      "entity_type": "Event",
      "rule": "Merge two Event records if they share the same LiveWhale 'id', LibCal numeric event ID, or Bedework ('guid', 'recurrenceId') pair. Across different platforms/URLs (such as events.columbia.edu + Eventbrite in col-01, or LibCal + primary host page in nyu-09), merge iff university matches, start_at overlaps within 15 minutes, resolved Place (or online modality) matches, and normalized core title/speaker matches. Keep repeating installments on different dates (weekly 'Meditations on Earth' in nyu-14, monthly 'Saturday Science' in col-01, repeated 'Introduction to Zotero' workshops in col-03, semesterly study breaks in nyu-10) as separate Event entities sharing only series_name; only bundle multiple dates into one Event.sessions array when a single production/market page explicitly lists those slots together (nyu-01, col-07)."
    },
    {
      "entity_type": "Organization",
      "rule": "Scope organization matching by university (leaving external partners unscoped). Merge records sharing a feed group ID ('gid' in LiveWhale; 'agrp_*'/'calsuite' in Bedework), or matching normalized names after stripping redundant parent prefixes ('Steinhardt Music and Performing Arts Professions' in nyu-15 == 'Music and Performing Arts Professions' under NYU Steinhardt in nyu-02), or matching parenthetical acronyms declared on official pages ('CUSP' in nyu-04, 'CRACS Co-Lab' in nyu-09, 'CUNO' in col-01). Keep sub-units distinct from parent schools/libraries via part_of_org rather than merging them."
    }
  ],
  "decisions": [
    {
      "choice": "Keep people and event series as fields on Event rather than separate Person and EventSeries entity types",
      "weighed": "Promoting Person and EventSeries to full entity types vs storing featured_people, contact, and series_name on Event.",
      "decision_and_why": "Kept them as Event fields. Across all 15 samples, no speaker or performer appears in more than one event, staff organizers carry no rich attributes ('No Profile image'), and recurring series (nyu-04, nyu-14, col-01) have no standalone URLs or IDs. Keeping just Event, Place, and Organization keeps the graph small, checkable, and free of stub entities."
    },
    {
      "choice": "Model Place at the building/venue level and keep rooms and virtual links on Event",
      "weighed": "Creating a Place entity per room or virtual link vs scoping Place to physical buildings/outdoor spaces and putting location_detail + modality on Event.",
      "decision_and_why": "Chose building-level Place plus Event.location_detail and Event.modality. Bobst Library hosts three different sample events in three different rooms (nyu-07, nyu-10, nyu-14); building-level Places avoid fragmenting campus landmarks and prevent bogus entities like 'Online Online' (col-03)."
    },
    {
      "choice": "Represent event timing as a non-empty sessions array with nullable end_at",
      "weighed": "Single start_at/end_at fields on Event vs separate Occurrence child entities vs an embedded sessions array on Event.",
      "decision_and_why": "Chose a sessions array on Event with nullable end_at. Thirteen samples have one slot (including nyu-15 with no end time), while nyu-01 (six play performances) and col-07 (six market afternoons) publish multiple slots on a single URL without per-slot pages."
    },
    {
      "choice": "Add explicit access_scope ('public' vs 'host_university_only') while excluding all student-side state",
      "weighed": "Copying raw Bedework/LibCal audience tag lists vs distilling cross-campus eligibility into access_scope.",
      "decision_and_why": "Distilled eligibility into optional access_scope and stored zero student/twin interaction data. Because NYU and Columbia twins share this base, knowing whether an event welcomes outside students (nyu-04 via Luma, col-01, col-05) or requires a host NetID/UNI (nyu-12, col-03) prevents twins from recommending inaccessible events across campuses."
    },
    {
      "choice": "Drop coordinates, thumbnails, and form-input metadata",
      "weighed": "Including lat/lon coordinates (nyu-05, nyu-15) and flyer thumbnails (nyu-05, nyu-15, col-01, col-05) vs dropping them.",
      "decision_and_why": "Dropped them. Coordinates appear in only 2 of 15 samples (below the 3-sample threshold), Bedework image paths are relative fragments, nyu-05's thumbnail filename references uninvolved speakers ('Anthony_Scaramucci__Manu_Meel'), and none help a low-token text twin verify facts."
    }
  ],
  "uncertain": [
